                %a{:href => "#triangulations_and_covers"} Triangulations and Covers
          %h2#classical_triangulations Classical Triangulations
          %h3#aim Aim
          %p The aim of this entry is to describe some of the classical versions of important concepts which are needed elsewhere. This may serve as an entry point for someone versed in a more classical version of algebraic topology, or being adept at the nPOV, and its ramifications, needs to bridge the gap to more classical ideas to understand some more classically written source. (It may also be useful if some classically written source is not at hand when you need it!) The exposition will be fairly ‘classical’ with asides to explain the significance for later developments and for connections to the nPOV.
          %h2#triangulations__lancienne Triangulations à l’ancienne
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polyhedron"} polyhedron
            (in the sense of polyhedral space), i.e. a space homeomorphic to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realisation"} geometric realisation
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complex"} simplicial complex
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong classical triangulation
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a pair
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (K,f)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a simplicial complex and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : |K|\to X
              is a homeomorphism.
          %p (In this context we will often drop the term ‘classical’ referring to ‘triangulation’ if there is little risk of confusion.)
          %h2#classical_subdivision Classical subdivision
          %p
            The older form of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subdivision"} subdivision
            involved the geometric realisation in the following way:
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a simplicial complex, a
              %strong (classical) subdivision
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a simplicial complex,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                          %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^\prime
            %p
              a) the vertices of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^\prime
              are (identified with) points of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
            %p
              b) if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^\prime
              is a simplex of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^\prime
              there is a simplex,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              such that
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                          %mo ′
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^\prime \subset |s|
            %p
              c) the mapping from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K^\prime|
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^\prime
              to the corresponding points of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
          %p
            The interpretation, in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complex"} simplicial complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
            as convex combinations of the vertices, allows an interpretation to be ascribed to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^\prime
          %h3#properties_of_classical_subdivisions Properties of Classical Subdivisions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Any subdivision of a subdivision of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                is a subdivision of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K'
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ″
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K''
                are subdivisions of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                then there is a subdivision
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ‴
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K'''
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                that is a subdivision of both
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K'
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo ″
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K''
          %p
            These statements thus assert that the subdivisions of a simplicial complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            form a directed set with respect to the partial ordering defined by the relation of subdivision. (We will return to this later in this entry.)
          %p
            Given any simplex,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in K
            (or put more pedantically
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S(K)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complex"} Canonical Construction
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
            = succeed "," do
              %em open simplex
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle s \rangle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complex"} simplicial complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
            is constructed as follows:
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
            is the set of all functions from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(K)
            to the closed interval
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in |K|
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≠
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v \in V(K) \mid \alpha(v)  \neq  0\}
          %p
            is a simplex of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %ul
            %li
              for each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\in V(K)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{\alpha \in V(K)} \alpha (v) = 1.
          %p
            (We then give this set a topology (see
            = succeed ").)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complex"} simplicial complex
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in K
              = succeed "," do
                %strong open simplex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle s \rangle\subset |K|
              is defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle s \rangle = \{ \alpha \in |K| \mid \alpha(v) \neq 0 \Leftrightarrow v\in s\}.
          %p
            Beware although a closed simplex will be a closed subset of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle s \rangle
            is and open set of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |s|
          %h2#barycentric_subdivision_classical_geometric_forms Barycentric subdivision (classical geometric forms)
          %p
            The barycentric subdivision is one of the best known and most useful natural subdivisions available in general. (Other are also used, for instance, the middle edge or
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+subdivision"} ordinal subdivision
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subdivision"} subdivision
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              If
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma = \{ v_0, \ldots, v_q\} \in K_q
              = succeed "-simplices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "," do
                %strong barycentre
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b(\sigma)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi i
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi q
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b(\sigma) = \sum_{0\leq i \leq q}\frac{1}{q + 1} v_i \in |K|.
            %p
              The
              = succeed "," do
                %strong barycentric subdivision
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sd
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sd K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is the simplicial complex whose vertices are the barycentres of the simplices of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              and whose simplices are finite non-empty collections of barycentres of simplices, which are totally ordered by the face relation of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(K)
          %p
            As
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b(\sigma)
            is completely determined by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_alternative_form Definition: (Alternative form)
            %p
              The
              = succeed "," do
                %strong barycentric subdivision
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sd
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sd K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is the simplicial complex specified by
            %ul
              %li
                the vertices of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sd
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sd K
                are the simplices of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %li
                the subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\sigma_0, \ldots \sigma_q\}
                is a simplex of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sd
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sd K
                if there is a total order on its elements (which will be assumed to be the given order, as written) such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi …
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi q
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_0\subset  \ldots \subset\sigma_q.
          %h2#triangulations_and_covers Triangulations and Covers
          %p We now need a bit more terminology:
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Given any vertex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %strong star
              is defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi st
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} st( v) = \{ \alpha \in |K| \mid \alpha(v)\neq 0\}.
          %p
            The set,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi st
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} st(v)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi st
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi v
                  %mtext is a vertex of
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} st(v) = \bigcup \{\langle s \rangle\mid\  v \text{ is a vertex of }s\},
          %p
            the union of the interiors of those simplices that have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            as a vertex. These vertex stars give an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |K|
            and the following classical result tells us that the nerve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\mathcal{U})
            of this covering is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            itself (up to isomorphism):
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_cf_spanier_p_114 Proposition (cf. Spanier, p. 114)
            %p
              Let
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi st
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U} = \{st(v)\mid v \in V(K)\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\mathcal{U})
              defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi st
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi (v) = \langle st(v)\rangle
            %p is a simplicial isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi K
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : K \cong N(\mathcal{U}).
